<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hatuniye Madrasa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1382</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Hatuniye Medrese</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hatuniye <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">Madrasa</a> is a theological college in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karaman">Karaman</a>, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, completed in 1382. It was founded by Nefise <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a>, a daughter of the Ottoman sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murad-i">Murad I</a> and wife of the Karamanid ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaeddin-bey">Alaeddin Bey</a>. Its richly carved marble portal makes it one of the finest buildings of the Karamanid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hatuniye-madrasa.jpg" alt="Hatuniye Madrasa" width="320" height="481" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dosseman · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karaman_Hatuniye_Medresi_4812.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
